{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 SGM Studios Essentials\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A set of REAPER utility scripts I use in my own sessions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Included: - SGM_route_mix_bus.lua \u8212- Route all tracks through a Mix Bus (dry-run safe) - SGM_auto_master.lua \u8212- One-click mastering chain with REAPER stock plugins - SGM_FieldyBagToggle.lua \u8212- Toggle between Fieldy/Dimebag bass FX chains - SGM_reaper_ultra_hd_smart_tools.lua \u8212- 4K-optimized theme with smart tools - daw-discovery-analyzer.lua \u8212- Profile your REAPER environment - SGM_Utils.lua \u8212- Shared utility library (loaded by other scripts)\par}

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Fieldy-Bag Toggle\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Toggles between two bass guitar FX chains: Fieldy (slap/rock) and Dimebag (metal). Requires the correct plugin ordering on the selected bass track.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b FX slot layout:} - Slots 1-3: Fieldy chain (Korn-style slap/rock bass) - Slots 4-6: Dimebag chain (Pantera-style metal bass)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b How it works:} - Running the script checks the state of slot 1 - If Fieldy is active (slots 1-3 enabled, 4-6 bypassed), switches to Dimebag (slots 4-6 enabled, 1-3 bypassed) - Run again to toggle back to Fieldy - Console shows which chain is now active\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b How to use:} 1. Select a bass track with FX in slots 1-6 2. Run the script 3. Check the console for the active chain name\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Edge cases handled:} - No track selected: shows error message - Track has fewer than 6 FX: toggles what\u8217's available gracefully - Track has no FX: shows message, no crash\par}

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 REAPER Auto Mastering Tool\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Applies a professional mastering chain to the master bus using built-in REAPER plugins (ReaEQ, ReaComp, ReaLimit).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Chain order:} 1. ReaEQ (High-Pass Filter at 30 Hz) \u8212- removes subsonic rumble 2. ReaComp \u8212- bus compression with configurable threshold 3. ReaLimit \u8212- peak ceiling at -1.0 dBTP\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b How to use:} 1. Run the script 2. If the master track has existing FX, a confirmation dialog appears 3. Click \u8220"Yes\u8221" to clear and reapply the mastering chain 4. Chain is applied in order: HPF \u8594 ? Compressor \u8594 ? Limiter\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Configuration (edit at top of script):} - HPF_FREQ = 30: high-pass filter frequency (Hz) - COMP_THRESH = -18: compressor threshold (dB) - COMP_RATIO = 2:1: compressor ratio - LIMIT_CEIL = -1.0: limiter ceiling (dBTP)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Edge cases handled:} - Existing FX: prompts before clearing - Cancel dialog: no changes made, no undo point created - Multiple runs: stacks FX (intentional for A/B comparison)\par}

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 REAPER Ultra HD Smart Tools\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 4K/UHD-optimized REAPER theme generator with WCAG-compliant contrast optimization and smart toolbar tools.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b What it does:} - Generates a 4K-optimized REAPER theme with high-contrast WCAG-compliant color palette (dark theme with Pro Tools-inspired blue accents) - Includes a defer loop for dynamic toolbar tools: - Toolbar clock display - CPU meter overlay - Color picker for track/item tinting - AI-aware UI elements with distinct colors for AI-suggested state\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b How to use:} 1. Run the script to apply the 4K theme 2. Run again to start the deferred toolbar tool loop 3. The defer loop runs until the script is terminated via Actions\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Limitations:} - Best results on REAPER 7.0+ (native 4K support) - Theme generation modifies the REAPER color scheme \u8212- backup your current theme before applying - Defer loop consumes minimal CPU but should be terminated when not needed - Some UI elements may need manual tweaking depending on your display configuration (DPI scaling, monitor setup)\par}

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 SGM Route Mix Bus\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Creates (or finds) a dedicated Mix Bus track, disables Master/Parent send on every other track, and routes them all through the Mix Bus. The Mix Bus itself feeds the Master \u8212- perfect for bus compression, overall mix glue, or stem-style mixing workflows.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Features:} - DRY_RUN mode: set DRY_RUN = true to preview changes without applying - Folder depth behavior: processes tracks at the specified folder depth - Duplicate-send prevention: skips tracks already routed to Mix Bus - Color-coded Mix Bus track (configurable RGB color)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b How to use:} 1. Select the tracks to route through the Mix Bus 2. Run the script 3. Check the console for a summary of routing changes\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Configuration (edit at top of script):} - MIX_BUS_NAME = \u8220"Mix Bus\u8221": name of the bus track - MIX_BUS_COLOR = \{ r = 255, g = 180, b = 50 \}: track color - DRY_RUN = false: set to true for preview mode - DEBUG = false: set to true for verbose logging\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Edge cases handled:} - No tracks selected: shows error \u8220"No tracks selected.\u8221" - Mix Bus already exists: reuses existing bus track - Already routed tracks: skips duplicate sends\par}

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 REAPER DAW Discovery and Analyzer\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Profiles the current REAPER installation and open project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b What it analyzes:} - Operating system and REAPER version - Audio device configuration (driver, sample rate, block size) - Available plugins (scans installed VST/VST3/AU/JSFX) - Track structure (count, routing graph, folder hierarchy) - Project settings (tempo, time signature, length) - System specs relevant to audio performance (CPU, RAM, disk)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Dependencies:} - Core features work without any external extensions - SWS/S&M Extension enables advanced routing inspection - Script detects SWS availability and adjusts output accordingly\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Output format:} - Clean, formatted console report - Sections: System Info, Audio Config, Plugin Inventory, Track Map, Routing\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b How to use:} 1. Open a REAPER project 2. Run the script 3. Open View \u8594 ? Console to read the report\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Edge cases handled:} - SWS not installed: routing features limited, note printed in report - Empty project: still reports system info and audio config - No plugins found: reports \u8220"No plugins discovered\u8221"\par}

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Rule of 30 Heavy Metal Production Bundle\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A complete session building system for professional heavy industrial and metal production in REAPER.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Includes: - rule-of-30-session-builder.lua: builds the full 48+ track session - rule-of-30-plugin-presets.lua: plugin chain configuration library (dependency) - phase-alignment-tool.lua: sample-accurate DI guitar alignment\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Drop Bb tuning. 95-110 BPM. Designed for dense, high-track-count productions with quad-tracked guitars, double bass, and full orchestral augmentation layers.\par}

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 SGM Studios \u8212- REAPER Scripts\par}
